## OSINT-Specific Considerations

### Data Source Management
- Prioritize reputable, verifiable sources
- Implement source credibility scoring
- Maintain comprehensive source metadata
- Track source reliability over time
- Flag potential misinformation or bias

### Privacy & Ethics
- Never store personally identifiable information unnecessarily
- Implement data anonymization for analytics
- Respect robots.txt and rate limiting
- Comply with data protection regulations (GDPR, CCPA)
- Clear user consent for data collection

### Verification Workflows
- Cross-reference information across multiple sources
- Timestamp all data collection for provenance
- Implement fact-checking integrations
- Flag unverified or disputed information
- Maintain audit trails for all data processing

## Technical Stack Preferences

### Frontend
- Vite + React 18 with TypeScript for type safety
- Tailwind CSS for styling
- React Context + useReducer pattern for state management
- Leaflet/react-leaflet for geographic visualization and mapping
- Lucide React for icons

### Backend
- Express.js for API server (current)
- Planned migration to Supabase for backend services
- PostgreSQL for structured data (articles, sources, users)
- Redis for caching and real-time features (future)
- Vector database for semantic search (future consideration)

### Infrastructure
- Docker for containerization
- Vercel or AWS for hosting
- GitHub Actions for CI/CD
- Sentry for error tracking
- Posthog or Mixpanel for analytics

### AI/ML
- Ollama for local/cloud LLM text analysis
- Custom keyword extraction for topic detection
- Custom embeddings for article similarity

